  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 9 December 2026 at 10:00AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nReleased to the market for the first time in 35 years, this superb property offers plenty of space and scope. Combining timeless 1950s craftsmanship with contemporary upgrades, the substantial family home on a level 1049m² (more or less) site delivers an enviable coastal lifestyle. Add to that the potential to build up to capture amazing sea views and you have something supremely special!\r\n\r\nPredominantly single level, the floor plan offers exceptional versatility with four bedrooms, two bathrooms, a study, multiple living zones (including a rumpus room) and a dedicated workshop. The interior spills out onto a large elevated deck with stairs leading down to a lawn that’s perfect for the kids to run around, kick a ball or set up a game of backyard cricket. A gate at the bottom of the garden provides pedestrian access to the beach - so morning swims and coastal walks can be part of your daily routine.\r\n\r\nThe location is outstanding and hard to replicate! It is within easy reach of numerous parks and reserves, the boat club, waterfront, shops, restaurants and amenities; also close to, and in zone for, Glendowie College and Primary.\r\n\r\nWords don’t do it justice. Suffice it to say, this is a rare opportunity that needs to be taken advantage of - without delay! Contact us today for a private viewing appointment or visit our upcoming open homes.\r\n\r\nPlease visit www.barfoot.co.nz/945004 and scroll down to download or view: Title; LIM (where available); Particulars and Conditions of Sale by Auction (where applicable); and other informative documents\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
